  "body": "What happens: the batch gate on `main` at `b65413b2` is red in one app test; the other eight steps (geometry, cl, tools, post, sim, motion, ui, clippy) are green.\n\nFailing test: `a_step_lathe_holder_placed_off_its_model_frame_is_judged_and_its_mirror_stands_clear` in `crates/app/tests/vendor_tool_body.rs` (panic at line 122; the suite's other 2 tests pass):\n\n```\npost blocked - the setup (F1): post Fanuc does not serve TestBench lathe, a turning machine - it would write a program that machine cannot run; give the setup a post that serves turning, or suppress its operations\n```\n\nReading: the test posts a turning setup through the generic Fanuc (milling) post, and the \"post serves the machine kind\" refusal now blocks that. The refusal looks right; the test's setup probably needs a post that serves turning. Two PRs that each passed alone seem to have met on main (the vendor tool model work, #1043 / `testdata/models/lathe_holder_offset.step`, and the post-serves-kind refusal). Which merge made it red was not bisected.\n\nEvidence: `gate-logs/batch-20261112-232427/07-app_suites_slow_release_tier_center_cut_multiaxis_.log` (around line 3999) on the maintainer's machine. Checkout did not move during the run (no VOID); no golden files changed.\n\nReproduce: `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test vendor_tool_body -- a_step_lathe_holder_placed_off_its_model_frame_is_judged_and_its_mirror_stands_clear --exact`\n\nDone means: that test passes on main with the refusal left in place (the test gets a turning post, or the correct fix if the refusal is wrong for this machine), and the batch tier is green again.\n",
